                <div id="tab55" class="content">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What are the "CA/CFA Pathway" mentioned in the title</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-1">The curriculum is structured to align with
                            the core content requirements for professional certifications like Chartered Accountant (CA)
                            and Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA). This allows students to simultaneously prepare for
                            these certifications alongside their degree, giving them a significant head start on their
                            professional qualification journey.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is it mandatory to choose a certification (CA or CFA) or sit for the
                                professional exams?
                            </p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-2">No, the decision to sit for the external
                            professional exams (CA or CFA) is entirely optional. The programme is designed to provide the
                            curriculum and preparation necessary for these pathways. However, the choice to pursue the
                            official certification, including registering for and taking the external exams, remains
                            with the student. Your undergraduate's degree from Masters' Union is a stand-alone qualification.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">When do I need to choose between the CA or the CFA pathway?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-3">The decision should be made before the
                            beginning of the course. We offer dedicated pre-enrollment guidance to help you make an
                            informed choice.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> Is switching from CA to CFA allowed?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>

                        <div class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-4">

                            <div class="detailsList faq-log">
                                <ul class="list">

                                    <p>
                                        Yes, in principle, it is allowed, but the process has two parts:
                                    </p>

                                    <li>
                                        <p>
                                            Internal Academic Flexibility (Masters' Union): If a student decides in the
                                            first year to switch their focus, then you will not lose the credits from
                                            your academic degree. However, we allow case by case basis in the first
                                            semester only.

                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <p>External Certification (ICAI/CFA Institute): This is the main point of
                                            clarity: you cannot switch credit between the two certification bodies. CA
                                            (ICAI) and CFA (CFA Institute) are independent, external qualifications.
                                            <br>If you pay the registration fee and clear a level of one (e.g., CA
                                            Foundation) and then switch to the other (CFA), you will have to start from
                                            Level I of the new certification. The fees paid for the first certification
                                            are non-transferable and non-refundable to the new certification.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>


                                </ul>

                            </div>
                        </div>

                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Is switching from CFA to CA allowed?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-5">No, this is not allowed given CA has a lot
                            of statutory components and a mandatory articleship.

                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-z-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading"> If a student fails a level of the CA or CFA exam, does it affect
                                their degree?</p>

                            <img src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer font-16 font-grey13" id="tab-z-6"> No, The UG Programme in Finance &
                            Economics is an independent academic degree. Your undergraduate's degree is awarded solely based
                            on your successful completion of the required academic coursework, internal exams, and
                            industry projects mandated by Masters' Union.<br> Failure in any level of the professional
                            examinations (CA or CFA) does not affect the student's academic standing or their ability to
                            graduate with the undergraduate's degree from Masters' Union.
                        </p>
                    </div>

